 ["What is the colored part of your eye called?","Iris","Pupil","Lens","Eyelid","The pupil is the black hole in the middle that lets light in."],
 ["What do the tiny hairs inside your nose do?","Catch dust and germs","Help you taste","Make your nose grow","Nothing at all","Your nose also warms and wets the air before it reaches your lungs."],
 ["What is the main job of your lungs?","Getting oxygen into your blood","Pumping blood","Digesting food","Making bones","Your left lung is a little smaller to make room for your heart."],
 ["About how long is your small intestine?","About 20 feet","About 1 foot","About 3 feet","About 100 feet","It's called \"small\" because it's skinny, not because it's short!"],
 ["What is the biggest organ inside your body?","Liver","Brain","Stomach","Heart","The liver can grow back if part of it is removed."],
 ["Which vitamin does your skin make when sunshine hits it?","Vitamin D","Vitamin C","Vitamin A","Vitamin K","Vitamin D helps your body build strong bones."],
 ["What kind of joint is your knee?","A hinge joint","A ball-and-socket joint","A pivot joint","A glue joint","Your shoulders and hips are ball-and-socket joints, so they can swing in circles."],
 ["What are your hair and fingernails made of?","Keratin","Calcium","Plastic","Bone","Animal horns, hooves, and claws are made of keratin too."],
 ["About how many times do you blink in one day?","About 15,000","About 100","About 1,000","About 1 million","Every blink spreads tears to keep your eyes clean and wet."],
 ["Which blood cells fight germs?","White blood cells","Red blood cells","Platelets","Brain cells","Platelets are the cells that help make a scab when you get a cut."],
 ["What does your stomach use to break down food?","Acid","Plain water","Tiny teeth","Air","Your stomach makes a fresh lining every few days so its own acid doesn't hurt it."],
 ["Which blood vessels carry blood back to your heart?","Veins","Arteries","Nerves","Tendons","Laid end to end, all your blood vessels could wrap around Earth more than twice!"],
 ["What does DNA do in your body?","It holds the instructions for building you","It fights germs","It carries oxygen","It helps you hear","The DNA in just one of your cells would stretch about 6 feet if you unwound it."],
 ["What are the small bones that make up your spine called?","Vertebrae","Ribs","Knuckles","Tendons","A giraffe and a person both have 7 bones in their neck."],
 ["What gives your skin, hair, and eyes their color?","Melanin","Blood","Sunlight","Freckles","Melanin also helps protect your skin from the Sun."],
 ["Where are your vocal cords?","In your throat","In your chest","In your nose","On your tongue","Your voice box is also called the larynx."],
 ["About how much does a grown-up's brain weigh?","About 3 pounds","About half a pound","About 10 pounds","About 20 pounds","Your brain uses about 20% of all your body's energy."],
 ["What causes goosebumps?","Tiny muscles pulling your hairs up","Your skin shrinking","Germs","Your blood freezing","Animals fluff up their fur the same way to stay warm or look bigger."],
 ["Which parts of your body hold more than half of all your bones?","Your hands and feet","Your skull","Your spine","Your ribs","Each of your hands has 27 bones."]
